"# TITLE: \"The Quantum Entanglement of Hollow Ridge\"\n\n## INTRODUCTION (3 minutes):\n\nKEEPER: Welcome to tonight's session of Delta Green. I'm your Keeper, Dakota Reynolds. Tonight we find ourselves in the present day, October 2023, in the remote town of Hollow Ridge, nestled in the Appalachian Mountains. A series of bizarre disappearances has drawn the attention of Delta Green, and a team has been assembled to investigate. Before we dive in, let's meet our agents.\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): I'm playing Marcus Blackwood, a forensic entomologist with the FBI's Behavioral Analysis Unit. He's in his early 40s, methodical and detail-oriented. After witnessing something unexplainable during a serial killer case in 2019, he was recruited into Delta Green. His cover within the Program is \"specialized evidence collection.\"\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): I'm playing Gabriela Montero, a forensic linguist with the Department of Homeland Security. She's 35, brilliant with languages and decoding patterns. She was brought into Delta Green after analyzing communications from a cult that seemed to contain impossible linguistic structures. She's pragmatic but curious to a fault.\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): I'm playing Vincent Hargrove, also a forensic entomologist with the FBI's BAU. He's 38, more impulsive than his colleague Marcus, and has a photographic memory for insect behavior patterns. He joined Delta Green after discovering parasitic organisms of unknown origin during a case in the Florida Everglades.\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): I'm playing Dominic Everhart, a quantum computing specialist with DARPA. He's 32, socially awkward but mathematically brilliant. He was recruited when his theoretical models predicted anomalous energy signatures that matched Delta Green field reports. He's the tech guy who's never quite comfortable in the field.\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): I'm playing Jasper Whitman, a forensic anthropologist with the Department of Defense. He's 45, a former military man with extensive field experience. He identified skeletal remains with impossible anatomical features during a classified operation, which led to his recruitment. He's the practical, grounded member of the team.\n\nKEEPER: Excellent. You've all been called in under various pretexts to investigate a situation in Hollow Ridge. Three people have vanished in the last month, all after reporting seeing strange lights near the old Quantum Research Facility that was supposedly decommissioned in 2015. Local authorities are baffled, and when one officer went missing while investigating, Delta Green took notice. Your handler, Agent ADAM, has provided you with cover as a special federal task force investigating potential environmental contamination. Let's begin.\n\n## SCENE 1 (7 minutes):\n\nKEEPER: It's a crisp autumn evening as your convoy of unmarked government vehicles winds through the mountain roads toward Hollow Ridge. The trees are ablaze with fall colors, but as you get closer to town, you notice patches of forest where the leaves have turned an unnatural blue-black color. You arrive at the local sheriff's office, a small brick building in the center of town. Sheriff Eliza Dawson, a stern-looking woman in her fifties, is waiting for you at the entrance.\n\nKEEPER: \"I appreciate the federal interest, but I'm not sure what you think you'll find that we haven't,\" Sheriff Dawson says as she leads you into a small conference room. \"Three missing persons in a month is unusual for us, but people go missing in these mountains all the time.\" She lays out three files on the table, each with a photo: Martin Wells, a local science teacher; Diane Cho, a hiker passing through the area; and Deputy Jim Larson, who went missing while investigating the second disappearance.\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): Marcus adjusts his glasses and opens the first file. \"Sheriff Dawson, we appreciate your cooperation. Did any of the missing individuals mention unusual experiences before their disappearances? Anything that seemed out of the ordinary, even if it sounds insignificant?\"\n\nKEEPER: The sheriff hesitates before answering. \"Well, Martin\u2014the teacher\u2014he'd been acting strange for about a week before he vanished. Talking about hearing buzzing sounds and seeing lights up near the old research facility. I figured he was just stressed from the new school year. Diane, the hiker, she asked some locals about 'the blue lights on the mountain' before she went missing. And Jim...\" She pauses. \"Jim called in on the radio the night he disappeared, said something about insects acting weird around the facility perimeter.\"\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): Vincent perks up at the mention of insects. \"What exactly did Deputy Larson report about the insects? Any specific behaviors or species he mentioned?\"\n\nKEEPER: \"He said they were swarming in geometric patterns. Said it looked deliberate, like they were forming symbols. I told him he was being dramatic.\" She looks uncomfortable. \"We found his patrol car the next morning, empty, with the driver's door open and his flashlight still on.\"\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): Jasper leans forward, studying the case files. \"Were there any physical traces left behind at any of the disappearance sites? Footprints, personal effects, signs of struggle?\"\n\nKEEPER: \"Nothing with Martin or Diane. With Jim, we found his service weapon on the ground about fifty feet from his car. It had been fired once. No blood, no shell casing. It's like he just... vanished.\" She pulls out a plastic evidence bag containing the deputy's pistol. \"You're welcome to examine it.\"\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): Dominic clears his throat nervously. \"I'd like to know more about this research facility. What kind of work were they doing there? And who owned it before it was decommissioned?\"\n\nKEEPER: The sheriff shrugs. \"It was some private outfit called Quantum Horizon. Very hush-hush. They claimed to be doing materials research, but they had government contracts. Lot of specialized equipment being trucked in and out. They shut down suddenly in 2015, laid off all the local staff with generous severance packages and NDAs. Place has been abandoned since then\u2014officially, anyway.\"\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): Gabriela takes notes as the sheriff speaks. \"Have you noticed any unusual communications in the area? Strange radio frequencies, interference patterns, or even changes in local speech patterns or terminology?\"\n\nKEEPER: Sheriff Dawson gives Gabriela an odd look. \"That's a strange question, but now that you mention it, we've had issues with radio communications near the facility. Cell service drops completely within about a mile radius, and radio gets this strange static that almost sounds like... whispering.\" She shakes her head. \"And there's been talk among the locals about 'the blue-black words.' Some kind of graffiti that's appeared in a few places around town. Nonsense symbols, but they give people headaches to look at them.\"\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): \"We'd like to see these symbols,\" Marcus says, exchanging a glance with Gabriela. \"And we'll need to visit the disappearance sites, starting with where Deputy Larson's vehicle was found.\"\n\nKEEPER: \"I can take you there now,\" the sheriff offers. \"It's about twenty minutes up the mountain road, at the edge of the old facility's property.\" As you prepare to leave, you notice a map of the area on the wall. The facility is marked, as well as a nearby cave system and an old fire watchtower on an adjacent peak.\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): Vincent studies the map carefully. \"Those caves connected to the facility in any way? And is the watchtower still in use?\"\n\nKEEPER: \"The caves run deep under this whole area. There were rumors that the facility had some underground sections that connected to them, but I can't confirm that. The watchtower hasn't been officially manned in years, but hikers use it sometimes for the view.\"\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): \"Let's head to the deputy's car location first,\" Jasper suggests. \"I'd like to examine the area before it gets dark.\"\n\nKEEPER: The sheriff leads you to your vehicles. As you drive up the winding mountain road, the radio begins to crackle with static. Through the interference, you can make out what sounds like whispered voices speaking in an unknown language. The patches of blue-black leaves become more frequent as you ascend. Finally, you arrive at a small turnout where police tape still cordons off an area. The deputy's car has been removed, but the scene is otherwise preserved.\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): Dominic pulls out a small device from his bag. \"I'm going to measure electromagnetic frequencies in the area.\" He makes a PHYSICS roll.\n\nKEEPER: Roll the dice for your Physics check, Avery.\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): I got a 65, which is under my Physics skill of 70. Success!\n\nKEEPER: Dominic's device begins registering unusual readings immediately. There's a consistent pattern of quantum fluctuations that, according to everything you know about physics, shouldn't be possible in a natural environment. The readings increase in intensity when pointed toward the facility, which you can now see in the distance\u2014a cluster of low, gray buildings surrounded by a chain-link fence.\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): Marcus kneels down to examine the ground where the deputy's car was found. \"I'm looking for any insect activity that matches what the deputy reported.\" I'll make an ENTOMOLOGY roll.\n\nKEEPER: Roll for it, Morgan.\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): That's an 82, which is a failure against my 85 Entomology.\n\nKEEPER: You find normal insect activity for the season, but nothing forming the geometric patterns the deputy reported. However, as you're searching, you notice something unusual\u2014a small patch of what appears to be blue-black residue on a nearby tree. It has a strange, iridescent quality that shifts when viewed from different angles.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): Gabriela approaches the tree. \"I want to examine this residue more closely, but not touch it directly.\" I'll use a sample collection kit from my field bag.\n\nKEEPER: As Gabriela collects a sample, you all notice that the whispered voices on the radio have grown louder. The sheriff, who has been watching from near her vehicle, suddenly calls out to you.\n\nKEEPER: \"Hey, do you see that?\" Sheriff Dawson points toward the facility. In the gathering dusk, faint blue lights can be seen flickering between the buildings. \"That's what Martin described seeing before he disappeared.\"\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): Vincent takes out his binoculars to get a better look at the lights. \"What exactly am I seeing here?\" I'll make a SPOT HIDDEN check.\n\nKEEPER: Roll for Spot Hidden, Rowan.\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): I rolled a 25, which is well under my 65 Spot Hidden.\n\nKEEPER: Through the binoculars, Vincent can see that the lights aren't fixed sources like lamps or flashlights. They appear to be swarms of tiny, luminescent insects moving in coordinated patterns. They're forming what look like complex mathematical equations or circuit diagrams in the air, constantly shifting and reforming. As you watch, the swarms seem to pulse in unison, and for a brief moment, you feel a strange pressure in your head, like someone is trying to push a thought into your mind.\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): Jasper notices Vincent's expression change. \"What do you see?\" He moves to take the binoculars.\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): Vincent lowers the binoculars, looking disturbed. \"Insects... but they're behaving impossibly. Forming patterns, equations. And there's something... something trying to communicate.\" He hands the binoculars to Jasper, rubbing his temples.\n\nKEEPER: As Jasper takes the binoculars, the radio in Sheriff Dawson's vehicle suddenly blares to life, the volume increasing dramatically. Through the static, a voice that sounds like Deputy Larson's can be heard saying, \"They're in the equations. The patterns. Don't look too long. They get in through your eyes.\" Then the radio dies completely.\n\n## SCENE 2 (7 minutes):\n\nKEEPER: The sun has now set completely, and the blue lights at the facility have grown more intense. Sheriff Dawson stands frozen by her vehicle, staring at the dead radio. \"That... that was Jim's voice,\" she says shakily. \"What the hell is going on here?\" Before anyone can answer, her phone rings. She answers it, listens for a moment, then turns to you with wide eyes. \"There's been another disappearance. A teenage boy, Kevin Mills. His friends say he went to the old watchtower to take pictures of the 'blue lights' and never came back. They found his camera at the base of the tower.\"\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): Jasper takes charge of the situation. \"We need to split up. Some of us should check out the watchtower while others investigate the facility. Sheriff, would you be willing to take some of us to the watchtower?\"\n\nKEEPER: The sheriff nods, still visibly shaken. \"I know these mountains well. I can guide a team to the watchtower.\"\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): \"I'll go to the facility with Vincent,\" Marcus says. \"Our entomology background might help us understand what we're seeing with these insect swarms.\"\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): \"I should go to the facility too,\" Dominic adds. \"Those quantum readings are strongest in that direction, and I need to get closer to understand what's happening.\"\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): \"I'll head to the watchtower,\" Gabriela decides. \"If there are more of those symbols or any kind of communication happening, I want to analyze it.\"\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): \"Are we sure splitting up is wise?\" Vincent asks, concerned. \"These disappearances happened to people who were alone.\"\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): \"Good point. No one goes anywhere alone. Gabriela and I will go with the sheriff to the watchtower. The rest of you head to the facility, but stay together at all times.\"\n\nKEEPER: You split into two groups. Marcus, Vincent, and Dominic begin making their way toward the facility, while Jasper and Gabriela follow Sheriff Dawson down a narrow hiking path toward the watchtower. Let's follow the facility team first.\n\nKEEPER: As Marcus, Vincent, and Dominic approach the perimeter fence of the facility, the blue lights seem to react to your presence, swirling more rapidly and converging near the main building. The fence itself appears to be intact, with \"NO TRESPASSING\" and \"GOVERNMENT PROPERTY\" signs posted at regular intervals. There's a main gate with a rusted padlock.\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): Dominic scans the area with his EM device. \"The quantum fluctuations are off the charts here. Whatever's happening inside is bending the laws of physics.\" He looks nervously at the lock. \"Should we try to get in?\"\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): \"We need to see what's inside,\" Marcus says, examining the lock. \"I have some basic lockpicking tools in my kit.\" I'll attempt a LOCKSMITH roll.\n\nKEEPER: Roll for it, Morgan.\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): I rolled a 92, which is a failure against my Locksmith skill of 40.\n\nKEEPER: The old lock resists your attempts, and after a few minutes of trying, one of your picks breaks off inside it.\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): \"Let me try something else,\" Vincent says. He examines the fence line carefully. \"Maybe there's another way in, or a section of fence that's been compromised.\" I'll make a SEARCH roll.\n\nKEEPER: Roll for Search, Rowan.\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): I got a 15, which is a success against my Search of 70.\n\nKEEPER: Vincent discovers a section of fence about thirty yards to the right of the main gate where something large appears to have pushed through from the inside, creating a gap just wide enough for a person to squeeze through. The metal is bent outward and has the same blue-black residue you found on the tree.\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): \"I don't like the implications of that damage pattern,\" Dominic says nervously. \"Something came out, not in.\"\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): \"Let's proceed with caution,\" Marcus says, taking out his service weapon. \"Dominic, stay between Vincent and me.\"\n\nKEEPER: As you squeeze through the gap in the fence, the swarms of luminescent insects become more agitated, forming complex, three-dimensional patterns in the air around you. The main building looms ahead\u2014a two-story concrete structure with few windows. The door is ajar, and a faint blue glow emanates from inside.\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): Vincent takes out a specimen container. \"I want to try to capture some of these insects for analysis.\" I'll make an ENTOMOLOGY roll to try to safely collect a few without disturbing the swarm pattern.\n\nKEEPER: Roll Entomology, Rowan.\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): I rolled a 30, success against my 85 Entomology.\n\nKEEPER: Vincent successfully captures several of the insects in a specimen container. Up close, they don't match any known species. They appear to be some kind of hybrid between fireflies and cicadas, but with an exoskeleton that has an almost metallic quality. The blue luminescence seems to pulse in time with each other, even when separated.\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): Dominic looks at the captured insects with fascination. \"They're exhibiting quantum entanglement properties. That shouldn't be possible in living organisms.\" He turns his attention to the building. \"We need to see what's inside.\"\n\nKEEPER: Let's switch to the watchtower team. Sheriff Dawson leads Jasper and Gabriela up a steep trail through increasingly dense patches of the blue-black foliage. Your flashlights illuminate the path, but the beams seem to be absorbed by the strange-colored leaves, creating odd shadows. After about fifteen minutes of hiking, you reach the base of the old fire watchtower\u2014a weathered wooden structure rising about forty feet above the rocky outcrop.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): Gabriela examines the area around the base of the tower. \"I'm looking for the camera that was mentioned, and any signs of the missing teenager.\" I'll make a SEARCH roll.\n\nKEEPER: Roll for Search, Sage.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): I got a 55, which is a success against my Search of 60.\n\nKEEPER: Gabriela finds the camera\u2014a digital SLR with an expensive telephoto lens\u2014partially hidden under some blue-black leaves. When you check the display, you find it's still on, showing the last image taken: a zoomed-in shot of the research facility with bright blue mathematical equations floating in the air above it. But there's something else in the image\u2014a tall, thin silhouette standing on the facility roof, surrounded by the swirling lights.\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): Jasper looks at the image over Gabriela's shoulder. \"What the hell is that?\" He turns to the sheriff. \"Has anyone reported seeing a figure like this before?\"\n\nKEEPER: Sheriff Dawson shakes her head, looking disturbed. \"No, nothing like that.\" She points to the base of the tower. \"Look at these markings.\"\n\nKEEPER: Around the wooden support posts of the tower, someone has carved or burned strange symbols into the wood\u2014complex, angular patterns that seem to shift slightly when viewed peripherally. They match the description of the \"blue-black words\" mentioned earlier.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): Gabriela approaches the symbols carefully. \"I want to document these and attempt to analyze their linguistic structure.\" I'll make a LINGUISTICS roll.\n\nKEEPER: Roll Linguistics, Sage.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): I rolled a 42, which is a success against my Linguistics of 85.\n\nKEEPER: As Gabriela studies the symbols, she realizes they form a complex mathematical language rather than a traditional linguistic system. It appears to be describing quantum states and interdimensional coordinates. With growing alarm, she recognizes that the symbols are actually a form of theoretical quantum programming language that was only theorized in classified papers\u2014it shouldn't exist in practical form. The most disturbing realization is that some of the symbols seem to be moving slightly, rearranging themselves as she watches.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): Gabriela steps back from the symbols, looking concerned. \"These are... they're a form of quantum programming language. They're describing coordinates or gateways between dimensions. And they're active\u2014they're changing as we watch.\"\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): \"We need to check the tower itself,\" Jasper says, shining his light up the wooden structure. \"If Kevin came here to take photos, he might have climbed up for a better view.\"\n\nKEEPER: The wooden stairs leading up the tower creak ominously as you begin to ascend. Sheriff Dawson follows behind you. About halfway up, you notice more of the symbols carved into the steps and railings, becoming more concentrated as you climb higher.\n\nKEEPER: Meanwhile, back at the facility, Marcus, Vincent, and Dominic have reached the main entrance. The door swings open at your touch, revealing a darkened reception area. Emergency lights powered by backup generators cast a dim glow over abandoned desks and fallen ceiling tiles. The air is thick with dust, except for clear pathways on the floor where something has been moving regularly.\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): Marcus sweeps his flashlight across the room. \"Look at the floor patterns. Something's been moving through here consistently, keeping those paths clear of dust.\" He follows one of the paths with his light. \"Where does this lead?\"\n\nKEEPER: The path leads to a set of double doors marked \"LABORATORY ALPHA - AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY.\" Through the small windows in the doors, you can see more of the blue light pulsing rhythmically.\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): Dominic's hands shake slightly as he reads the quantum fluctuation measurements on his device. \"Whatever is generating these readings is behind those doors. The patterns suggest some kind of sustained quantum field that's... folding space-time.\"\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): \"Before we go in there,\" Vincent says, \"let's check if there's a security office or records room. We need to understand what they were working on here.\"\n\nKEEPER: A quick search reveals a small security office off to the side of the reception area. Inside, you find powered-down monitors and an old desktop computer. There's also a logbook and a set of facility blueprints spread out on the desk.\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): \"I'll try to get this computer running,\" Dominic says, sitting down at the desk. \"It might have security footage or research data.\" I'll make a COMPUTER SCIENCE roll.\n\nKEEPER: Roll Computer Science, Avery.\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): I rolled a 38, success against my Computer Science of 90.\n\nKEEPER: Dominic manages to boot up the old computer. After bypassing the password protection, you access the security system. Most of the camera feeds are offline, but one camera is still active\u2014showing the interior of Laboratory Alpha. The footage reveals a large chamber dominated by what appears to be a quantum computer setup, but modified in ways you've never seen before. Blue energy arcs between the processing units, and in the center of the room, suspended in mid-air, is what can only be described as a tear in reality\u2014a vertical, shimmering rift about seven feet tall that pulses with the same blue light you've seen outside.\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): \"My God,\" Marcus whispers, staring at the screen. \"They've opened something.\"\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): Vincent grabs the facility blueprints. \"Let's see if there's another way into that lab, or if there are any other areas we should be aware of.\" I'll examine the blueprints with a SEARCH roll.\n\nKEEPER: Roll Search, Rowan.\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): I rolled a 72, which is a failure against my Search of 70.\n\nKEEPER: The blueprints are complicated and partially redacted. You can make out the main layout of the facility, including Laboratory Alpha, but many of the underground sections are marked only as \"CLASSIFIED\" with no details. You do notice that there appears to be a connection to the cave system mentioned earlier, marked as \"Natural Formation Access - Restricted.\"\n\nKEEPER: Back at the watchtower, Jasper and Gabriela have reached the observation platform at the top. The view is spectacular\u2014you can see the research facility clearly about a mile away, its outline illuminated by the swirling blue lights. But what draws your attention is what's on the platform itself. A circle of the strange symbols has been carved into the wooden floor, and in the center lies a small device that looks like a cross between a smartphone and a scientific instrument.\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): Jasper approaches carefully but doesn't touch the device. \"Sheriff, have you ever seen anything like this before?\"\n\nKEEPER: Sheriff Dawson shakes her head. \"Never. But...\" She points to something small next to the device. \"That's Kevin's class ring. He was definitely here.\"\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): Gabriela studies the circle of symbols. \"This is a more complex version of what we saw below. It's like... a receiving station or amplifier for whatever is happening at the facility.\" I want to take photos of everything and then examine the device without touching it.\n\nKEEPER: As Gabriela takes photos, the device suddenly activates, its screen lighting up with the same blue glow. Symbols begin scrolling across the screen, and a mechanical voice speaks: \"Calibration complete. Quantum entanglement established. Awaiting final coordinates for full manifestation.\"\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): \"That doesn't sound good,\" Jasper says, backing away. \"Gabriela, any idea what this thing is doing?\"\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): \"It's communicating with whatever is happening at the research facility,\" she says tensely. \"I think it's part of a system to... open something. A doorway or portal of some kind.\"\n\nKEEPER: Suddenly, Sheriff Dawson gasps and points toward the facility. \"Look!\"\n\nKEEPER: A column of intense blue light has erupted from the research facility, shooting straight up into the night sky. The swarms of luminescent insects are now forming a massive, complex pattern in the air above the facility\u2014a pattern that matches the symbols carved into the watchtower floor.\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): \"We need to warn the others,\" Jasper says urgently, pulling out his phone. \"And we should get this device. It might be crucial to understanding what's happening.\" I'll make a SAN roll to see if I can bring myself to touch the device.\n\nKEEPER: Roll Sanity, Phoenix.\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): I rolled a 35, which is under my current Sanity of 65.\n\nKEEPER: Jasper steels himself and carefully picks up the device. It feels unusually warm and seems to vibrate slightly in your hand, but otherwise appears to be a sophisticated piece of technology. The screen continues to display scrolling symbols.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): Gabriela tries calling the others. \"We need to tell them what we've found and warn them about that light.\"\n\nKEEPER: Your call doesn't go through\u2014just static and what sounds like whispering voices. At that moment, the device in Jasper's hand beeps loudly and displays a message: \"CONVERGENCE IMMINENT. PREPARE FOR ARRIVAL.\"\n\n## SCENE 3 (7 minutes):\n\nKEEPER: We return to the facility team. Marcus, Vincent, and Dominic have just witnessed the security footage showing the rift in Laboratory Alpha when the entire building shudders. The blue light intensifies dramatically, visible even through the small windows in the security office. Dust falls from the ceiling as the vibrations increase.\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): \"We need to get to that lab now,\" Marcus says urgently. \"Whatever's happening is accelerating.\"\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): Dominic looks terrified but resolute. \"My readings indicate a massive spike in quantum fluctuations. If that rift is expanding, it could potentially engulf the entire facility... or worse.\"\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): \"Let's move,\" Vincent says, leading the way out of the security office. \"But stay alert. We don't know what else might be in here with us.\"\n\nKEEPER: As you make your way toward Laboratory Alpha, following the clear paths in the dust, you hear a strange chittering sound coming from ahead. Rounding a corner, you come face to face with what appears to be a man in a lab coat, standing perfectly still in the corridor. As your flashlights illuminate him, you realize with horror that his body is serving as a host for thousands of the luminescent insects, which are crawling in and out of his mouth, eyes, and ears. His eyes are open but entirely blue, glowing with the same light as the insects.\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): Marcus raises his weapon instinctively. \"Federal agents! Don't move!\" I'll make a SAN roll.\n\nKEEPER: Roll Sanity, Morgan.\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): I rolled a 75, which is a failure against my current Sanity of 70.\n\nKEEPER: Marcus loses 1d4 Sanity points from witnessing this horrific sight.\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): I rolled a 3, so I'm down to 67 Sanity.\n\nKEEPER: The figure doesn't respond to Marcus's command. Instead, it tilts its head at an unnatural angle, and the insects form patterns in the air around it that resemble the symbols you've seen. A voice emerges\u2014not from the figure's mouth, but seemingly from the collective buzzing of the insects: \"The convergence has begun. The Mathematician will soon arrive.\"\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): Dominic is frozen in terror. \"W-what is the Mathematician?\" he stammers. I'll also make a SAN roll.\n\nKEEPER: Roll Sanity, Avery.\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): I rolled a 92, which is a failure against my Sanity of 60.\n\nKEEPER: Dominic loses 1d6 Sanity points.\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): I rolled a 4, down to 56 Sanity.\n\nKEEPER: The insect-voice responds to Dominic's question: \"The Mathematician exists between dimensions, calculating the equations of reality. It has found this universe suitable for expansion of its theorem. Your minds will serve as processing nodes in its grand calculation.\"\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): Vincent studies the insect swarm with professional interest despite his fear. \"These insects... they're extensions of this entity? Biological quantum processors?\" I'll make an ENTOMOLOGY roll to understand what I'm seeing.\n\nKEEPER: Roll Entomology, Rowan.\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): I rolled a 22, success against my Entomology of 85.\n\nKEEPER: Vincent realizes these aren't just insects\u2014they're hybrid organisms, partially insectoid but with elements that suggest artificial construction. They appear to function as a hive mind, but also as biological quantum bits\u2014qubits\u2014capable of maintaining entanglement across distances. The human host is essentially being used as a biological antenna and power source.\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): \"It's using the insects as a quantum computing network,\" Vincent explains quickly. \"And that... person... is being used as a biological router or power source. We need to get past it to reach the lab.\"\n\nKEEPER: The figure suddenly steps aside, as if inviting you to proceed. \"The Mathematician welcomes observers to its emergence. Your presence has been calculated and found acceptable.\"\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): Marcus keeps his weapon trained on the figure as they move past. \"Stay together. Don't touch anything or anyone.\"\n\nKEEPER: You cautiously make your way past the insect-infested figure, which remains motionless except for the constant movement of insects through its body. As you approach the doors to Laboratory Alpha, the blue light becomes almost blinding. Through the windows, you can see that the rift has grown larger, now about ten feet tall and shimmering with intense energy.\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): \"The quantum field is destabilizing,\" Dominic warns, checking his device. \"Whatever's on the other side of that rift is starting to come through.\"\n\nKEEPER: Meanwhile, at the watchtower, Jasper, Gabriela, and Sheriff Dawson are making their way back down as quickly as possible. The device in Jasper's hand continues to display \"CONVERGENCE IMMINENT\" as the column of blue light from the facility grows wider and brighter.\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): \"We need to get to the facility,\" Jasper says as they descend. \"Whatever's happening is centered there.\"\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): Gabriela studies the device as they move. \"This might be a control mechanism or at least connected to whatever process is occurring. If we can understand it, maybe we can interrupt the convergence.\" I'll make a SCIENCE roll to try to decipher its function.\n\nKEEPER: Roll Science, Sage.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): I rolled a 31, success against my Science of 65.\n\nKEEPER: Gabriela determines that the device is indeed a control mechanism\u2014specifically, it's calibrating and stabilizing the quantum field being generated at the facility. The scrolling symbols are coordinates and parameters for the dimensional rift. There appears to be an emergency shutdown protocol, but it would require entering the correct sequence of symbols.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): \"I think I can shut this down,\" Gabriela says excitedly. \"But we'd need to be closer to the facility for it to work\u2014the quantum entanglement weakens with distance.\"\n\nKEEPER: As you reach the base of the watchtower, Sheriff Dawson suddenly stops and points to the tree line. \"There's someone there!\"\n\nKEEPER: A figure emerges from the trees\u2014it's a teenage boy matching Kevin Mills' description, but like the figure in the facility, his body is host to swarms of the luminescent insects. His eyes glow blue, and he moves with an unnatural, jerky gait.\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): \"Kevin?\" Jasper calls out cautiously, positioning himself between the boy and Gabriela.\n\nKEEPER: The Kevin-thing tilts its head, and the insects form patterns around him. \"Kevin Mills has been integrated into the calculation. His neural pathways now serve the Mathematician.\" The voice has the same buzzing quality as the one in the facility.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): Gabriela works frantically on the device. \"I need to decode this shutdown sequence. Keep him talking or distracted.\" I'll make a LINGUISTICS roll to decipher the symbol pattern needed.\n\nKEEPER: Roll Linguistics, Sage.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): I rolled a 12, a solid success against my Linguistics of 85.\n\nKEEPER: Gabriela quickly identifies the pattern needed for the shutdown sequence. It's complex but followable\u2014a mathematical proof that seems designed to contradict the equations being used to open the rift. You'll need to input this sequence when you're closer to the facility.\n\nKEEPER: Back at the facility, Marcus, Vincent, and Dominic stand before the doors to Laboratory Alpha. The insect-infested figure has followed you and now stands silently behind, blocking your retreat.\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): \"We need to see what's coming through that rift,\" Marcus says grimly. \"Ready?\"\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): Vincent nods. \"Let's do it.\"\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): \"Wait,\" Dominic says, checking his device one last time. \"The quantum signature just changed. Something is actively coming through now.\"\n\nKEEPER: Marcus pushes open the doors to Laboratory Alpha. Inside, the modified quantum computer hums with power, blue energy crackling between its components. The rift hovers in the center of the room, now large enough for something to step through. As you watch, a tall, impossibly thin figure begins to emerge\u2014a being with a form that seems to shift between humanoid and geometric, its \"skin\" covered in constantly moving mathematical equations and symbols identical to those you've seen throughout your investigation. Where its face should be is a complex, three-dimensional mathematical formula that hurts your eyes to look at directly.\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): \"My God,\" Marcus whispers. \"Is that... the Mathematician?\" I need to make another SAN roll, I assume.\n\nKEEPER: Yes, roll Sanity, Morgan.\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): I rolled a 42, which is a success against my current Sanity of 67.\n\nKEEPER: You maintain your composure despite the impossible sight before you. The being continues to emerge, more of its impossible geometry becoming visible in our reality. The air around it seems to warp and distort.\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): \"The quantum computer,\" Vincent says suddenly. \"It must be powering the rift. If we can shut it down...\" I want to look for any emergency shutdown controls.\n\nKEEPER: Roll SPOT HIDDEN, Rowan.\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): I rolled a 50, success against my Spot Hidden of 65.\n\nKEEPER: Vincent notices an emergency shutdown panel on the wall near the quantum computer. It's protected by a keycard reader and what appears to be a biometric scanner.\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): \"I might be able to bypass the security,\" Dominic offers. \"But I'll need time.\" He moves toward the panel, trying to avoid drawing attention from the emerging entity.\n\nKEEPER: Outside the facility, Jasper, Gabriela, and Sheriff Dawson have reached the perimeter fence. The Kevin-thing has followed at a distance, occasionally stopping to allow more insects to enter and exit its body. The column of blue light now connects the facility to what appears to be a distortion in the night sky above.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): \"We need to get inside,\" Gabriela says urgently, holding up the device. \"I've figured out the shutdown sequence, but we need to be closer to the source.\"\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): Jasper spots the gap in the fence that the others used earlier. \"This way. Stay close and watch for more of those... hosts.\"\n\nKEEPER: As you squeeze through the fence, the Kevin-thing suddenly darts forward with inhuman speed, grabbing Sheriff Dawson by the arm. She screams as insects begin to crawl from his hand onto her skin.\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): \"Let her go!\" Jasper shouts, drawing his service weapon. I'll fire a warning shot to try to distract it. I'll make a FIREARMS roll.\n\nKEEPER: Roll Firearms, Phoenix.\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): I rolled a 27, success against my Firearms of 75.\n\nKEEPER: The warning shot strikes near the Kevin-thing's feet. It pauses, tilting its head curiously, but doesn't release the sheriff. The insects continue to spread up her arm as she struggles.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): \"The main entrance,\" Gabriela points. \"We need to get inside now!\"\n\nKEEPER: Inside Laboratory Alpha, the Mathematician has now emerged halfway through the rift. Its impossible geometry causes small objects in the room to float and distort. The insect swarms form complex patterns around it, seemingly in response to its presence.\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): Dominic works frantically at the emergency shutdown panel. \"I need a keycard or something to bypass this!\" I'll make a COMPUTER SCIENCE roll to try to hack it.\n\nKEEPER: Roll Computer Science, Avery.\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): I rolled an 81, which is a failure against my Computer Science of 90.\n\nKEEPER: Dominic's attempts to bypass the security are unsuccessful\u2014the system requires both a physical keycard and biometric authentication. As you work, the Mathematician turns its \"face\" toward you, and you feel an overwhelming pressure in your mind, as if complex equations are being forcibly inserted into your thoughts.\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): \"The host,\" Marcus says suddenly, pointing to the insect-infested figure that followed them. \"It might have access. It was wearing a lab coat\u2014it might be one of the original researchers.\"\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): Vincent approaches the insect host cautiously. \"We need to access the emergency shutdown. Can you assist us?\"\n\nKEEPER: The host tilts its head, and the insect-voice responds: \"The convergence cannot be stopped. The Mathematician has calculated all variables, including your resistance.\"\n\nKEEPER: At that moment, the doors to the laboratory burst open, and Gabriela and Jasper rush in, followed by Sheriff Dawson, who is desperately trying to brush insects from her arm.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): \"I have the shutdown sequence!\" Gabriela shouts, holding up the device. \"But we need to connect it to the main system!\"\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): Jasper quickly assesses the situation, seeing the emerging entity. \"What the hell is that thing?\"\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): \"The Mathematician,\" Marcus says grimly. \"Dominic, can that device Gabriela has interface with the quantum computer?\"\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): Dominic examines the device quickly. \"Yes! It's designed to communicate with this system. But we still need to bypass the security on the emergency shutdown panel.\"\n\nKEEPER: The Mathematician is now three-quarters emerged from the rift. Its presence is causing reality to warp around it\u2014the walls of the laboratory seem to bend and twist, and everyone feels a strange pressure building in their minds. Sheriff Dawson collapses to her knees, clutching her head as more insects begin to crawl over her body.\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): Vincent turns to the insect host again. \"Your calculations are incomplete. The Mathematician hasn't accounted for this device.\" He gestures to what Gabriela is holding. \"Help us, or your theorem will be flawed.\"\n\nKEEPER: Roll PERSUADE, Rowan.\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): I rolled a 40, success against my Persuade of 55.\n\nKEEPER: The insect host pauses, the swarm around it shifting patterns rapidly as if processing this new information. After a moment, it approaches the emergency panel and places its hand on the biometric scanner. The panel lights up green and slides open, revealing a manual override system.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): Gabriela rushes forward with the device. \"I need to connect this and input the shutdown sequence!\" She begins to interface the device with the override system.\n\nKEEPER: As Gabriela works, the Mathematician fully emerges from the rift. It stands nearly eight feet tall, its impossible form now fully visible in our reality. It raises what might be considered arms, and the quantum computer's components begin to float into the air, rearranging themselves around the entity.\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): \"It's integrating with the quantum computer,\" Dominic says in horror. \"If it completes that process, it will have enough processing power to fully stabilize in our reality.\"\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): \"How much longer, Gabriela?\" Jasper asks urgently, keeping his weapon trained on the Mathematician, though he suspects it would have little effect.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): \"Almost there,\" Gabriela says, fingers flying over the device's interface. \"The sequence is complex... I need to get it exactly right.\"\n\nKEEPER: The Mathematician turns its attention to Gabriela, seemingly aware of what she's attempting. The pressure in everyone's mind increases painfully as it focuses on her. Insects begin to swarm toward her position.\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): \"Cover Gabriela!\" Marcus shouts, moving to intercept the insect swarm. \"Don't let them reach her!\"\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): Vincent grabs a fire extinguisher from the wall. \"The insects don't like cold!\" He begins spraying the advancing swarm, creating a barrier of cold CO2.\n\nKEEPER: Roll DEX, Rowan.\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): I rolled a 35, success against my DEX of 60.\n\nKEEPER: Vincent successfully creates a barrier of cold CO2, temporarily dispersing the insect swarm. The Mathematician's form flickers slightly, as if the disruption of its insect extensions has affected its stability in our reality.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): \"Got it!\" Gabriela exclaims. \"Initiating shutdown sequence... now!\"\n\nKEEPER: The device connects fully with the override system, and Gabriela inputs the complex mathematical proof that contradicts the Mathematician's equations. The quantum computer begins to power down, and the rift starts to fluctuate wildly. The Mathematician's form distorts and stretches, as if being pulled back toward the rift.\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): \"It's working!\" Dominic shouts over the increasing noise of reality trying to reassert itself. \"The quantum field is collapsing!\"\n\nKEEPER: The Mathematician emits a sound that isn't quite audible\u2014more like a mathematical concept forced into sonic form. The insect hosts, including the partially-converted Sheriff Dawson, suddenly collapse to the ground as their controlling insects fall dormant. The rift begins to shrink, pulling the Mathematician back toward it.\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): \"Is it over?\" Jasper asks, helping Sheriff Dawson to her feet and brushing the now-motionless insects from her.\n\nKEEPER: As the rift continues to shrink, the Mathematician makes one final effort. It extends what might be an arm toward Gabriela, and for a brief moment, complex equations flood her mind\u2014glimpses of other dimensions and mathematical truths beyond human comprehension.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): Gabriela staggers under the mental assault. I'll make a SAN roll.\n\nKEEPER: Roll Sanity, Sage.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): I rolled a 95, which is a failure against my Sanity of 75.\n\nKEEPER: Gabriela loses 1d6 Sanity points as the alien mathematics temporarily overwhelms her mind.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): I rolled a 5, down to 70 Sanity.\n\nKEEPER: With a final reality-bending distortion, the Mathematician is pulled back through the rapidly closing rift. The quantum computer components crash to the floor as gravity reasserts itself, and the blue light fades. The rift shrinks to a pinpoint and vanishes with a sound like air rushing to fill a vacuum. The facility is suddenly eerily quiet, lit only by emergency lighting and your flashlights.\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): Marcus rushes to Gabriela's side. \"Are you alright? What happened?\"\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): Gabriela blinks, looking dazed. \"It... showed me things. Equations. Realities. I can't... quite hold onto them.\" She shakes her head. \"But I think it's gone. For now.\"\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): Vincent checks on the fallen insect host. \"This one's dead. The insects were keeping it alive somehow.\"\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): Dominic examines the now-dormant quantum computer. \"The system's completely fried. Whatever connection was established has been