tates. \"Some of them are already fading from my memory, like my mind can't hold onto them.\"\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): \"What about the missing people?\" Jasper asks. \"And the long-term effects on Sheriff Dawson and the Mills boy?\"\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): \"And the insect samples,\" Vincent adds. \"They're like nothing I've ever seen\u2014hybrids with both biological and artificial components.\"\n\nKEEPER: Agent ADAM nods grimly. \"The missing persons will be classified as presumed dead, lost in the mountains. Standard cover story. As for Sheriff Dawson and the boy, they'll be monitored discreetly. The insect samples and all other evidence are being transported to a secure facility for analysis.\" He looks at each of you seriously. \"The official story is that this was an abandoned research facility where illegal chemical experiments were conducted, resulting in hallucinations and environmental contamination. A hazmat team is handling the cleanup. The town will be compensated for environmental damages.\"\n\nKEEPER: As the sun rises higher, casting long shadows through the trees, you watch as Delta Green operatives systematically dismantle and pack away all evidence of what really happened here. The blue-black patches of foliage are being carefully removed and contained. In the distance, the old watchtower is being examined by another team.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): Gabriela looks thoughtful. \"The Mathematician... it wasn't destroyed, was it? Just sent back.\"\n\nKEEPER: \"Correct,\" Agent ADAM confirms. \"And now we know it's aware of our reality. The shutdown sequence you implemented was effective, but temporary. The entity will likely seek other ways to establish a presence here.\" He hands each of you a small pill. \"Standard amnestic. It won't erase everything, just blur the most sanity-threatening details. Recommended, but not mandatory for agents of your clearance level.\"\n\nPLAYER 1 (MORGAN): Marcus pockets the pill without taking it. \"Some things we need to remember, no matter how difficult.\"\n\nPLAYER 3 (ROWAN): \"Agreed,\" Vincent says. \"If it tries to come back, we need to be ready.\"\n\nPLAYER 4 (AVERY): Dominic looks at the pill uncertainly. \"I'm not sure I want to forget. The mathematics I glimpsed... it was beautiful, in a terrifying way.\"\n\nPLAYER 5 (PHOENIX): \"The question is,\" Jasper says quietly, \"who helped it the first time? Someone modified that quantum computer. Someone knew what they were opening a door to.\"\n\nKEEPER: Agent ADAM's expression remains neutral. \"That's an ongoing investigation. You'll be contacted if your expertise is needed.\" He gestures to the vehicles waiting to transport you away from Hollow Ridge. \"For now, your mission is complete. Well done, agents.\"\n\nKEEPER: As you leave Hollow Ridge behind, the cleanup operation continuing in your wake, each of you knows that the equations and symbols of the Mathematician have left their mark\u2014not just on the town and its unfortunate victims, but on your own minds. Some patterns, once seen, can never be completely forgotten. And somewhere, beyond the boundaries of our reality, the Mathematician continues its calculations, searching for another way in.\n\nPLAYER 2 (SAGE): Gabriela stares out the window as they drive away. \"Mathematics is the language of the universe,\" she says softly. \"But some equations were never meant to be solved.\"\n\nKEEPER: And with that chilling thought, we conclude tonight's session of Delta Green: \"The Quantum Entanglement of Hollow Ridge.\" Thank you all for playing, and remember\u2014some knowledge comes at a cost."